  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bharat Narayan Gadekar vs The State Of Maharashtra on 14 July, 2022 Author: S.G. Mehare Bench: S.G. Mehare 911-aba-860-2022.o (1) In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No.860 Of 2022 Bharat Narayan Gadekar ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent ... Mr. Himmatsinh D. Deshmukh, Advocate for the applicant. Mr. A.A. Jagatkar, App for the respondent-State. ... Coram : S.G. Mehare, J. Dated : 14th July, 2022. Per Court:-",
    "facts": "Therefore, nothing is to be recovered from him. Hence, he may be released on interim anticipatory bail. On the same observations, the learned Sessions Judge declined the bail to the applicant. Therefore, he is not entitled to the interim protection. The police had apprehended the applicant with the prohibited Gutka but did not registered any crime immediately nor called the Food and Drugs Inspector to lodge the report.",
    "arguments": "4. The learned APP has strongly opposed the application contending that the applicant did not respondent to the notice under Section 41-A of the Criminal Procedure Code. Issuing a notice under Section 41-A of the Criminal Procedure Code does not assure of no arrest of a person whom the said notice is served.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. The learned APP has strongly opposed the application contending that the applicant did not respondent to the notice under Section 41-A of the Criminal Procedure Code.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Issuing a notice under Section 41-A of the Criminal Procedure Code does not assure of no arrest of a person whom the said notice is served."
  },
